            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In 2 patients different coronary anomalies concerning the left coronary artery are reported, both patients having atypical angina-like chest pain; the indications for coronary bypass surgery are discussed, based on our understanding of the pathophysiology leading to myocardial ischemia.</AbstractText>
